<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <%-include("shared/meta")-%>
        <link href="https://www.legendhub.org/privacy.html" rel="canonical">
    </head>
    <body>
        <%-include("shared/header")-%>
        <main class="container">
            <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
            <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> August 30, 2026</p>
            <p>
                LegendHUB is a community resource for LegendMUD players. This policy
                explains what information LegendHUB handles, why it is used, when it
                may be disclosed, and the choices available to you.
            </p>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-information">
                <h2 id="privacy-information">Information we handle</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Account information:</strong> your username, email
                        address if one is provided, password hash, email-verification
                        status, login and session records, permissions, notification
                        settings, and other account preferences. LegendHUB does not
                        store your password in plain text.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Builder information:</strong> character profiles and
                        Builder preferences. Anonymous and unverified Builder data is
                        stored in your browser. If you use verified account storage,
                        selected Builder profiles and preferences are stored on the
                        LegendHUB server so they can follow you between devices.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Content and feedback:</strong> game information,
                        revisions, change notes, feedback titles, and feedback
                        descriptions that you choose to submit. Contributions may be
                        associated with your username. Feedback submitted through the
                        feedback form becomes a public GitHub Issue, so do not include
                        private information in it.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Technical and security information:</strong> cookies,
                        session identifiers, verification and recovery records, request
                        paths and response metadata, and network information used to
                        prevent abuse. LegendHUB stores hashed versions of IP addresses
                        for login and account-security controls.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-use">
                <h2 id="privacy-use">How we use information</h2>
                <p>LegendHUB uses information only to:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>operate, maintain, secure, and troubleshoot the site;</li>
                    <li>create accounts, authenticate users, and manage sessions;</li>
                    <li>verify email addresses and provide password recovery;</li>
                    <li>save preferences, notifications, and account-backed Builder data;</li>
                    <li>display and maintain user-submitted game information;</li>
                    <li>respond to feedback and requests; and</li>
                    <li>detect spam, automated traffic, fraud, and other abuse.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    LegendHUB does not sell or rent personal information and does not
                    use it for advertising, targeted marketing, or cross-site behavioral
                    tracking.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-disclosure">
                <h2 id="privacy-disclosure">When information is disclosed</h2>
                <p>
                    LegendHUB does not share personal information for advertising or
                    marketing. Limited information may be disclosed in these situations:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Services needed to operate LegendHUB:</strong> hosting,
                        private backup, and email-delivery providers may process the
                        information necessary to provide those services.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Google reCAPTCHA:</strong> registration and feedback use
                        reCAPTCHA to reduce automated abuse. Google processes information
                        under its
                        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
                        and <a href="https://policies.google.com/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Public GitHub feedback:</strong> when you submit feedback,
                        its title and description are sent to GitHub and published as an
                        Issue. GitHub handles that information under its
                        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">Privacy Statement</a>.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Legal and safety needs:</strong> information may be
                        disclosed when reasonably necessary to comply with a valid legal
                        obligation or to protect LegendHUB, its users, or others from
                        fraud, abuse, or a security threat.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-browser-storage">
                <h2 id="privacy-browser-storage">Cookies and browser storage</h2>
                <p>
                    LegendHUB uses cookies for sign-in, preferences, timezone display,
                    notification behavior, and remembering cookie or reminder choices.
                    The Builder also uses browser local storage for device-local
                    characters and migration acknowledgements. See the
                    <a href="/cookies.html">Cookie Policy</a> for more information.
                    You can remove cookies and local storage through your browser, but
                    doing so may sign you out, reset preferences, or delete Builder data
                    that exists only in that browser.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-retention">
                <h2 id="privacy-retention">Retention and deletion</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Active account information is retained until you request account
                        deletion.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Session, verification, recovery, rate-limit, and security records
                        are retained for their operational lifetimes and removed or
                        replaced as they expire or are no longer needed.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Account-backed Builder data is retained until you delete it,
                        delete the account, or request deletion. Deleting Builder data
                        removes its active stored payload.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Private disaster-recovery backups may contain account information.
                        Information deleted from the active system may remain in those
                        private backups until the backups are retired. Backups are used
                        for recovery and security, not to restore an individually deleted
                        account during ordinary operation.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Public game contributions and GitHub feedback may remain public
                        after account deletion. Contact LegendHUB if you also want a
                        specific public contribution or feedback Issue reviewed for
                        removal.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-choices">
                <h2 id="privacy-choices">Your choices and requests</h2>
                <p>
                    Account Settings lets you update your email address, password,
                    notification settings, and Builder storage. Builder data can be
                    exported or deleted from Account Settings. Browser-only information
                    can be removed through your browser controls.
                </p>
                <p>
                    To request access to, correction of, or deletion of your account
                    information, email
                    <a href="mailto:rufus@legendmud.org">rufus@legendmud.org</a>.
                    LegendHUB may need to verify that the request concerns your account.
                    Rights may also vary depending on where you live.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-security">
                <h2 id="privacy-security">Security</h2>
                <p>
                    LegendHUB uses technical and operational safeguards intended to
                    protect account information, including password hashing, hashed
                    session validators, access controls, private backups, and encrypted
                    web connections. No internet service can guarantee absolute security.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-children">
                <h2 id="privacy-children">Children</h2>
                <p>
                    LegendHUB is not directed to children under 13 and does not knowingly
                    collect personal information from them. A parent or guardian who
                    believes a child provided personal information should contact
                    <a href="mailto:rufus@legendmud.org">rufus@legendmud.org</a> so it
                    can be reviewed and deleted.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-signals">
                <h2 id="privacy-signals">Do Not Track signals</h2>
                <p>
                    LegendHUB does not use personal information for cross-site behavioral
                    advertising. Because necessary site operation does not change based
                    on a browser's Do Not Track signal, LegendHUB does not respond
                    differently when that signal is enabled.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-changes">
                <h2 id="privacy-changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
                <p>
                    This policy may be updated when LegendHUB's features or information
                    practices change. The effective date above will be updated, and
                    material changes will be announced through the site or changelog.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-contact">
                <h2 id="privacy-contact">Contact</h2>
                <p>
                    Questions or privacy requests can be sent to
                    <a href="mailto:rufus@legendmud.org">rufus@legendmud.org</a>.
                </p>
            </section>
        </main>
        <%-include("shared/footer")-%>
        <%-include("shared/scripts")-%>
    </body>
</html>
